<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khazar Khaganate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khazar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khazar Khaganate was a Turkic steppe state that controlled the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, the Caspian and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> from the seventh to the tenth century. Emerging from the western fringes of the Gokturk world, it grew wealthy from trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the Islamic world and the northern forests. Its ruling elite notably adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, and it declined after attacks by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> in the tenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate.jpg" alt="Khazar Khaganate" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chasaren.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
